.TH ATHENAEUM 1 "June 2026" "Athenaeum" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
athenaeum \- single-binary EPUB, PDF and audiobook library server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B athenaeum
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B athenaeum users
.I command
.RI [ flags "] [" args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Athenaeum
is a fast, self-hosted EPUB, PDF and audiobook library server that ships as a
single static binary with the web frontend embedded into the executable by
default. Use
.B \-\-web\-dir
to serve a filesystem SPA build instead.
Point it at a directory of media and it serves a web reader with full-text
search, collections, optional multi-user authentication, an OPDS catalog feed,
reading-progress sync and light/dark theming.
.PP
On startup
.B athenaeum
creates the data and library directories if they do not exist, opens (or
creates) the SQLite database under the data directory, scans the library and
serves HTTP on the configured address. On first visit an admin account can be
created in the browser setup wizard, or bootstrapped with
.B \-\-admin\-user
and
.BR \-\-admin\-pass .
.SH OPTIONS
Each flag has a corresponding environment variable; the flag takes precedence
when both are set.
.TP
.BI \-\-addr " address"
HTTP listen address.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_ADDR .
Default:
.BR :8080 .
.TP
.BI \-\-library " dir"
Root directory scanned for books.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_LIBRARY .
Default:
.BR ./library .
.TP
.BI \-\-data " dir"
Directory for the SQLite database and cover cache.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_DATA .
Default:
.BR ./data .
.TP
.BI \-\-web\-dir " dir"
Serve the frontend from this directory instead of the assets embedded in the
binary. The directory must contain
.IR index.html
(Vite production output). Empty uses the embedded build.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_WEB_DIR .
.TP
.BI \-\-admin\-user " name"
Create an admin user with this username on startup, only when no users exist
yet.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_ADMIN_USER .
.TP
.BI \-\-admin\-pass " password"
Password for the bootstrap admin user. Requires
.BR \-\-admin\-user
and a minimum length of 8 characters.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_ADMIN_PASS .
.TP
.BI \-\-upload\-max\-bytes " n"
Maximum upload size in bytes.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_UPLOAD_MAX_BYTES .
Default:
.BR 2147483648 " (2 GB)."
.TP
.BI \-\-scan\-workers " n"
Parallel library index workers.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_SCAN_WORKERS .
Default:
.BR 2 .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
Log verbosity:
.BR debug ", " info ", " warn ", or " error .
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_LOG_LEVEL .
Default:
.BR info .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " path"
Append logs to this file in addition to stderr.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_LOG_FILE .
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging (shortcut for
.BR \-\-log\-level=debug ).
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_DEBUG .
.TP
.BI \-\-color " mode"
CLI color mode:
.BR auto ", " always ", or " never .
Respects
.B NO_COLOR
and
.BR FORCE_COLOR .
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_COLOR .
Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color (same as
.BR \-\-color=never ).
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_NO_COLOR .
.TP
.BI \-\-sandbox " mode"
Linux Landlock and seccomp-bpf sandbox:
.BR off ", " try ", or " strict .
.B try
applies when the kernel supports it and continues on failure.
.B strict
fails startup if sandboxing cannot be applied.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_SANDBOX .
Default:
.BR off .
.TP
.B \-\-sandbox\-landlock
Enable Landlock filesystem restrictions when sandbox is on.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_SANDBOX_LANDLOCK .
Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.B \-\-sandbox\-seccomp
Enable seccomp-bpf dangerous-syscall denylist when sandbox is on.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_SANDBOX_SECCOMP .
Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Seed a generated demo library with books, audiobooks, and covers.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_DEMO .
.TP
.B \-\-self\-check
Verify that the binary can create and read/write the library and data
directories, open the database, start HTTP, and answer
.BR /api/health ,
then exit. Temporary directories are used unless
.B \-\-data
/
.B \-\-library
are set. Also available as
.B athenaeum self\-check
or
.BR athenaeum doctor .
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B self-check
Same as
.BR \-\-self\-check .
.TP
.B users
Manage local user accounts in the database without starting the server. See
.BR athenaeum-users (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I {data}/athenaeum.db
SQLite database (books, search index, users, collections, progress).
.TP
.I {data}/covers/
Cached cover images extracted from library files.
.TP
.I {data}/uploads/
In-progress resumable upload parts, removed once uploads complete.
.TP
.I {data}/i18n/
Custom locale JSON files.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.BR .epub ", " .pdf ", " .mp3 ", " .m4b ", " .m4a ", " .ogg ", " .flac .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Serve a library on all interfaces:
.B athenaeum \-\-addr :8080 \-\-library /path/to/books \-\-data ./data
.TP
Verify the binary can start and use its directories:
.B athenaeum \-\-self\-check
.TP
Bootstrap an admin account on first run:
.B athenaeum \-\-admin\-user admin \-\-admin\-pass 'your\-secure\-password'
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR athenaeum-users (1)
.PP
Project documentation: the bundled README and
.B GET /api/docs
(public JSON API reference).
